            <div xml:id="ch19">

                <pb facs="0622" n="520" xml:id="pg520"/>

                <head>Supplementary extradition treaties signed between the United States and
                    certain other countries</head>
                <p>[See telegraphic instruction of March 10, 1934, 1 p.m., to the Ambassador in
                    France, <ref target="frus:frus1934v01/pg_794">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1934, volume I, page
                        794</ref>; supplementary extradition treaties of the nature described in
                    that instruction were signed in 1935 between the United States and the following
                    countries: <list>
                        <item>Belgium, June 20, Treaty Series No. 900; 49 Stat. 3276.</item>
                        <item>Czechoslovakia, April 29, Treaty Series No. 895; 49 Stat. 3253.</item>
                        <item>Luxembourg, April 24, Treaty Series No. 904; 49 Stat. 3355.</item>
                        <item>Poland, April 5, Treaty Series No. 908; 49 Stat. 3394.</item>
                        <item>Switzerland, January 10, Treaty Series No. 889; 49 Stat. 3192.]</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
